Provenance
  engine/        The statistics engine of RINK-VT 2.5.0-rinkvt.1, the reference edition (the HERMIT gateway and
                 RINK-VT statistics terminal), by the same author: the command language, frames, game actor,
                 models, roster importer and the HK001 laboratory, as source files, unchanged by this edition
                 except where the reference edition itself changed them for it (a host-kept league), and for
                 the start frame (START) added in 2.5.0-lkvexa.2, which keeps every earlier behaviour.
  engine/rink/hk001/
                 Contains code derived from the Go standard library; its notices and licence terms are kept in
                 engine/rink/hk001/NOTICE.md and continue to apply to those parts.
  photon/        The Photon host follows the design of VEC1 Photon (Design Photon 0.6.0, Generic Photon 0.2.0,
                 WindowsSafe-r1, Copyright 2026 RUSSELL PHILIP SMITHSON, GPL-3.0-only): a Python control
                 plane, a Chromium-family renderer window on an isolated profile, a loopback JSON API guarded by
                 Host, Origin and a per-launch token, and a release-integrity gate. No Photon source file is copied.
  contracts/     MSSL 0.3 records in the observed subset described by the MSSL Writers Corpus 1.0.0, and JA Core
                 0.3 contract sources in the provisional grammar of the JA21 JA Core Application Language Suite
                 1.0.0 (both Copyright 2026 RUSSELL PHILIP SMITHSON, GPL-3.0-only). Neither corpus is bundled.
                 The JA sources are modeled contracts: no JA Core parser, compiler or VM is supplied or claimed.

Data
  The four demonstration clubs and every simulated game are fictional. HK001 is a deterministic synthetic
  research laboratory; it gives no forecasts, odds, or roster, medical, scouting or officiating advice.

